# Self-connect test: can the phone's STA join the SoftAP it is hosting?
# Measured 2026-11-27 20:57 on the XPLORE 2. Answer: no.
# Hotspot "XPLORE 2" on ap0 (5 GHz, 5180 MHz), BSSID 2a:aa:b4:59:d3:a0.

$ ip -4 -o addr show ap0
43: ap0    inet 10.105.197.112/24 brd 10.105.197.255 scope global ap0
$ dumpsys wifi | grep -A3 mCurrentSoftApConfiguration
mCurrentSoftApConfiguration: ssid = "XPLORE 2"
 bssid = 2a:aa:b4:59:d3:a0
 Passphrase = <non-empty>
 HiddenSsid = false

# The phone never sees its own beacon: 0 hits for its own SSID or BSSID.
$ cmd wifi list-scan-results | grep -c "XPLORE 2"
0
$ cmd wifi list-scan-results | grep -c "2a:aa:b4:59:d3:a0"
0

# Force a client connect to its own BSSID anyway. This is shell-legal:
# WifiServiceImpl.connect() has no self-SSID/self-BSSID check.
$ cmd wifi connect-network "XPLORE 2" wpa2 <redacted> -b 2a:aa:b4:59:d3:a0

# WifiClientModeImpl event log (dumpsys wifi):
rec[10] 20:57:13.634 CMD_CONNECT_NETWORK ... nid=5 cuid=2000 suid=2000 "XPLORE 2"WPA_PSK
rec[11] 20:57:13.651 CMD_START_CONNECT ... targetBssid=2a:aa:b4:59:d3:a0
rec[14] 20:57:13.656 SUPPLICANT_STATE_CHANGE_EVENT ... nid: 5 ... state: SCANNING
rec[18] 20:57:20.443 NETWORK_NOT_FOUND_EVENT ... ssid="XPLORE 2"
rec[24] 20:57:32.594 NETWORK_NOT_FOUND_EVENT ... ssid="XPLORE 2"

# 24 s later: still scanning, never ASSOCIATED, no wlan0, toggle still 0.
$ cmd wifi status | head -4
Wifi is enabled
Wifi scanning is always available
==== Primary ClientModeManager instance ====
Wifi is not connected
$ settings get global adb_wifi_enabled
0
$ ip -4 -o addr show wlan0
(no output)
$ getprop service.adb.tcp.port
5555

# 5555 was already there from the USB tcpip bootstrap. The point of this run is
# the toggle: it stayed 0, so on a cold boot this path would never let Keeper
# pin the port. The radio cannot receive the beacon it is transmitting.

# Rollback:
$ cmd wifi forget-network 5
Forget successful
